TITechTemplate.summary.ArrivalInternationalRelations=Earth nations consider their alignments as alien ships traverse the Solar System.<br/><br/><b>Economic Equalization Overhaul:</b> Reduces the Control Point economy-exponent score by 0.02.
TITechTemplate.summary.UnityMovements=Political scientists redraw nations that bring like-minded cultures together to maximize geopolitical power.<br/><br/><b>Economic Equalization Overhaul:</b> Reduces the Control Point economy-exponent score by 0.03.
TITechTemplate.summary.GreatNations=Unified nations spanning continents can bring massive economic and military power to bear on their rivals.<br/><br/><b>Economic Equalization Overhaul:</b> Reduces the Control Point economy-exponent score by 0.05.
TITechTemplate.summary.ArrivalGovernance=We explore ways to improve execution of law and policy in the new era.<br/><br/><b>Economic Equalization Overhaul:</b> Reduces the Control Point economy-exponent score by 0.05.
TITechTemplate.summary.Accelerando=We consider our prospects in a galaxy apparently teeming with aggressive life.<br/><br/><b>Economic Equalization Overhaul:</b> Reduces the Control Point economy-exponent score by 0.05.
TITechTemplate.description.NuclearFusioninSpace=Practical deuterium-tritium fusion and tritium breeding have proven that an off-world fusion power system can produce net energy and sustain its own fuel cycle. We must now turn that success into a family of robust reactor and propulsion architectures.<br/><br/>Our researchers are systematizing the ways that plasma can be confined, compressed, heated, and directed. Magnetic mirrors offer a direct first step, while static electric fields, inertial ignition, toroidal tokamaks, and Z-pinch compression each promise different combinations of output, efficiency, mass, and stability. No single method is sufficient for every spacecraft or habitat.<br/><br/>By treating deuterium-tritium fusion as the experimental foundation rather than the final design, we can develop the specialized methodologies needed for increasingly powerful reactors, drives, and advanced fusion fuel cycles.
